TI  - EFFECT OF SUPPLEMENTATION OF PROBIOTIC BACILLUS COAGULANS UNIQUE IS-2 ON HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA SUBJECTS: A CLINICAL STUDY
PY  - 2011
AB  - The objective of this study was to evaluate the effect due to consumption of capsule containing Bacillus coagulans Unique IS-2, on serum lipids for 60 days. Thirty hyperlipidemic (Having serum cholesterol levels of more than 200mg/dl) subjects were divided into 3 groups (n=10). Two group subjects were allotted to receive a daily dose of two capsules of probiotic Bacillus coagulans Unique IS2 (10X10 9 CFU/ capsule (Group A) and 20X10 9 CFU/capsule (Group B)) and third group subjects were received standard medication. Serum lipid profile was done at 0, 30 and 60 th day of the study period. At the end of study there were slightly reductions in total cholesterol (11%) and LDL (0.8%), whereas an increase in HDL cholesterol levels (3.6%). This data suggest that the strain Bacillus coagulans IS-2 has the potential of control in the serum cholesterol in humans suffering with hyperlipidemia.
